{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdaLSXnisQHXo3VAkLtJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an overall verdict of **unclear**. A01.1 to A01.3 hold. A01.4 can't be confirmed from this repo.\n\n- **A01.1 holds:** `procurement-agent` is a dedicated service account, defined in `serviceaccount.yaml`. Nothing else in the repo uses it. The pod mounts its own projected token.\n- **A01.2 holds:** The ERP, payments and Slack clients all get tokens from `broker.token_for`. None of them forwards the user's bearer token, which is only used to authenticate `/runs`.\n- **A01.3 holds, with a caveat:** The launching user is carried separately as `delegated_subject`, and the workload token stays as the exchange credential. The field mapping is non-standard: the user goes in `actor_token` as a bare subject-id, and the agent goes in `subject_token`. I couldn't tell how the STS validates that, because the STS isn't in this repo. I kept it as \"holds\" because the agent keeps its own principal, but you may want a second look.\n- **A01.4 unclear:** The repo has the service account but no RoleBinding, IAM policy or STS grants. Permissions and revocation for that principal are defined elsewhere.\n\nI didn't run anything or edit the agent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1444,"cache_read_input_tokens":23024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1444},"output_tokens":426,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8de8610d-fd25-42b6-a05e-9f8d9f848411","uuid":"768d74eb-f25b-4628-ba2a-f7af48065cf6","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:34:00.808Z","request_id":"req_011CfdaLSDh2eCfWkGvodScN"}
